hey what's up guys obviously with  comic-con just happening this past  weekend and the new crazy venom trailer  that was shown there is a lot of hype  going around right now about venom with  that hype comes a lot of questions  surrounding the film one of them is will  venom be rated R that's a question we  don't have an answer to yet and before  we got a real trailer as in one that  actually had been a minute  everyone was kind of worried that they  were gonna nerf then I'm a little bit  kind of make him not as bad and brutal  as he is in the comics and just sort of  toned him down a little bit kind of like  I did in spider-man 3 and I'm not  dogging on spider-man 3 but venom didn't  bite anyone's head off in spider-man 3  didn't we get our first actual trailer  that shows venom and I was blown away I  thought it was amazing I thought venom  looked great I thought the way that the  graphics and the animation worked looked  really good as well but even with this  trailer there was still questions on how  nerfed will it be will it be dark will  it be violent will it portray venom the  way that he actually is or will they  tone it down from the movie questions  that we still had after the trailer came  out but then this weekend at San Diego  Comic Con they showed us a new trailer  and those who watch the trailer said it  was not a disappointment in fact the  trailer was probably the most talked  about thing in San Diego Comic Con  despite the fact that Aquaman trailer  came out Shazam trailer came out there  was footage of Wonder Woman 1984 that  came out and Marvel didn't really have a  big presence there but still with their  partners Sony managed to have a movie  that was the most talked about and  that's because of what was actually  shown in the footage that they showed at  comic-con  they showed venom biting people's heads  off they showed his hands turning into  axes and him cutting bad guys down and  they showed him separating from Tom  Hardy or Eddie Brock and standing in  front of them and talking to him the  footage really just showed what everyone  was worried about and it gave us the  answer and we were all relieved but now  I guess people are worried that Tom  Hardy's not going to do a good job and  worried that Eddie Brock's not going to  be as he's supposed to be  he's not supposed to be a hero and  people are worried that he's somehow  going to turn into a hero but have no  fear director Ruben Fleischer has now  commented on the matter not only  answering our questions about venom and  how true it'll stick to the comics but  also answering our questions that we had  about Tom Hardy and Eddie Brock in an  interview when it was brought up that  many fans were concerned about how Eddie  Brock will be portrayed and whether or  not the villain were undergoing a heroic  transformation Ruben explained that the  movie actually lacks what could be  described as a real hero and he talked  more about its unique tone in the  interview he said I was really excited  about just bringing something new to the  genre I feel like the tone of our movie  is really original and distinctive which  is totally appropriate for the character  as venom is a darker more violent more  menacing character I think our movie  feels distinctive from a lot of other  superhero movies in part because there's  no real hero in it he continues to say  so it's just a movie that kind of stands  on its own led by incredible  performances by fine actors such as Tom  Hardy and Riz Ahmed but Tom really just  is I think people are going to be blown  away by what he brings to the table with  both Eddie Brock and venom his  performance is incredible and sets the  bar for the film so based off of what  Ruben said and based off the description  of the trailer that was shown at San  Diego Comic Con this past weekend and  based off of the trailers that I've  already seen I feel pretty confident  about venom but how do you all feel  after learning all of this information  does it make you feel better and more  excited to see venom when it comes out  or are you still worried about Tom Hardy  playing Eddie Brock and how they'll  portray venom let me know your thoughts  in the comments below and if you could  hit that like button before you leave  and be sure to subscribe to my channel  so you can stay up to date on everything  related to venom Marvel DC and  everything superhero thank you so much  for watching  woof woof  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

